WEBVTT

00:11.340 --> 00:14.390
<i>I was hoping it was all a dream, but...</i>

00:19.090 --> 00:21.990
<i>It looks like I really am in another world.</i>

00:24.250 --> 00:26.590
Hey, newbie, you're awake.

00:26.590 --> 00:27.580
You've got guests.

00:27.870 --> 00:28.610
Huh?

00:29.760 --> 00:31.720
Usato! Thank goodness you're okay.

00:31.720 --> 00:35.380
We were worried since we 
heard you'd been abducted.

00:35.380 --> 00:39.140
Sorry for worrying the two of you.

00:39.140 --> 00:40.880
I'm alive for n—

00:47.060 --> 00:49.480
<b>Ding</b>

00:47.390 --> 00:49.760
I'm supposed to start the 
training from hell today,

00:49.760 --> 00:52.000
so I can't say how tomorrow will go...

00:52.000 --> 00:54.860
Hell? Is it really that bad?

00:54.860 --> 00:56.060
Who knows?

00:56.060 --> 00:59.660
But it seems like you intend 
to go through with it.

00:59.660 --> 01:01.830
Well, yeah, I guess.

01:01.830 --> 01:03.990
I've got nothing better to do.

01:04.380 --> 01:08.590
And, if possible, I'd like to be of some use.

01:10.000 --> 01:12.280
I'd expect no less of you, Usato-kun.

01:12.280 --> 01:14.950
We begin our training today, as well.

01:14.950 --> 01:16.590
Let's all do our best!

01:17.350 --> 01:18.400
Yeah!

01:18.400 --> 01:22.070
I wonder what kind of cool 
training our heroes get to do.

01:22.430 --> 01:24.980
Your uniforms look pretty awesome.

01:26.100 --> 01:27.400
You think so?

01:29.340 --> 01:31.070
Thank you, Usato.

01:31.070 --> 01:33.480
I've finally made up my mind.

01:33.480 --> 01:34.650
Huh?

01:34.650 --> 01:38.080
Senpai, I'm going to do my best in this world.

01:38.350 --> 01:40.770
Good. I'll do the same.

01:42.230 --> 01:43.530
I received some gifts.

01:42.370 --> 01:45.160
<i>I'm sure Kazuki's going through a lot.</i>

01:43.530 --> 01:44.760
There's so much!

01:45.710 --> 01:49.720
<i>He was suddenly brought to another 
world and told he was a hero.</i>

01:49.720 --> 01:51.590
<i>And Inukami-senpai, too...</i>

01:52.470 --> 01:54.790
<i>No, she's probably fine.</i>

01:55.660 --> 02:00.140
<i>Anyway, I hope I can grow strong 
enough to support them someday.</i>

02:04.460 --> 02:06.190
The heroes already left?

02:07.480 --> 02:10.100
Did you enjoy your chat with them, Usato?

02:10.100 --> 02:11.910
Y-Yes, Ms. Rose!

02:11.910 --> 02:13.560
Thank you very much!

02:13.560 --> 02:17.520
This isn't a prison. 
You're free to see whoever you wish.

02:18.510 --> 02:21.200
When you're not training, that is.

02:21.200 --> 02:22.770
Y-Yes, ma'am.

02:22.770 --> 02:24.060
Take this.

02:25.110 --> 02:26.560
It's a journal.

02:26.560 --> 02:31.400
You should record your daily training 
regimen and how you feel about it.

02:31.400 --> 02:32.970
It'll prove useful.

02:33.210 --> 02:35.190
We'll get started after breakfast.

02:38.480 --> 02:42.020
<i>The training from hell is really starting...</i>

02:56.570 --> 03:01.240
<i>The Wrong Way to Use Healing Magic</i>

04:12.100 --> 04:15.900
#2 The Training from Hell Begins!

04:15.900 --> 04:22.820
<b>Day 1</b>

04:15.900 --> 04:22.820
<b>Day 1</b>

04:16.130 --> 04:20.210
<i>Day one. Tong and the others 
told me this training would be hell,</i>

04:20.210 --> 04:22.390
<i>but it was easier than I expected.</i>

04:23.080 --> 04:25.580
How is it? Do you feel anything?

04:26.130 --> 04:27.250
Yes.

04:27.250 --> 04:31.920
I feel some kind of warmth right here...

04:31.920 --> 04:33.600
That's mana.

04:33.600 --> 04:38.110
Next, you need to work on
 drawing that out of your body.

04:38.110 --> 04:40.960
Out of my body?

04:40.960 --> 04:42.430
You'll understand soon enough.

04:42.430 --> 04:44.810
For now, just focus on sensing it.

04:44.810 --> 04:46.100
Okay...

04:46.530 --> 04:47.500
Read.

04:47.500 --> 04:51.380
I can't read the language
 of this world, though.

04:51.380 --> 04:53.180
Just open the book.

04:58.670 --> 05:00.770
I can read it... I can actually read it!

05:01.120 --> 05:03.250
I heard that summoned heroes

05:03.250 --> 05:06.490
automatically have translation 
magic cast on them.

05:06.490 --> 05:08.870
You could've told me that sooner...

05:09.560 --> 05:11.630
This is the Llinger Kingdom.

05:12.430 --> 05:15.550
And this... is demon territory.

05:16.630 --> 05:18.260
It's right next door.

05:18.260 --> 05:19.230
Yes.

05:19.230 --> 05:22.850
That's why our kingdom 
is always their first target.

05:23.410 --> 05:25.020
Read that book.

05:25.020 --> 05:27.260
It has basic information about the nations,

05:27.260 --> 05:30.160
different races, and demons of this world.

05:30.160 --> 05:31.120
Okay.

05:35.630 --> 05:39.440
<i>If this is what the training is, 
I should be able to handle it.</i>

05:40.560 --> 05:44.230
<b>Day 2</b>

05:40.560 --> 05:44.230
<b>Day 2</b>

05:41.370 --> 05:44.240
<i>Day two. I ran a lot.</i>

05:47.390 --> 05:50.410
<i>This is magic training?</i>

05:50.410 --> 05:52.770
<i>It's different from what I expected...</i>

05:55.000 --> 05:57.410
<b>Day 3</b>

05:55.000 --> 05:57.410
<b>Day 3</b>

05:56.090 --> 05:57.410
<i>Day three.</i>

05:57.410 --> 06:00.920
<i>I was forced to run until my muscles 
were so sore that I couldn't move.</i>

06:05.560 --> 06:08.510
Hey, who said you could stop?

06:08.510 --> 06:09.920
I-I can't go on...

06:09.920 --> 06:11.310
My legs are done for...

06:11.980 --> 06:13.690
Ow! Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

06:13.690 --> 06:15.550
The pain is multiplied 
'cause I'm already hurt!

06:15.980 --> 06:16.980
Wait...

06:17.810 --> 06:19.400
It doesn't hurt.

06:19.740 --> 06:22.440
I healed your sore muscles.

06:22.440 --> 06:25.270
Huh?! You can do that?!

06:25.270 --> 06:28.030
Now get back to running, you piece of trash.

06:28.460 --> 06:29.620
Trash?

06:30.070 --> 06:32.500
I'm gonna die... She's gonna kill me!

06:33.390 --> 06:36.310
Run like you're going to die. 
I'll revive you if you do.

06:36.310 --> 06:38.020
<i>That doesn't even make sense!</i>

06:38.020 --> 06:40.310
<i>Of course, I can't say that out loud.</i>

06:40.310 --> 06:42.550
<i>Okay, I'll write it in my journal!</i>

06:42.670 --> 06:45.460
<b>Day 4</b>

06:43.860 --> 06:47.610
<i>Day four. I've started training 
with the other members.</i>

06:50.230 --> 06:52.940
Catch you later, Usato!

06:52.940 --> 06:55.170
You've got a long way to go, Usato!

06:55.170 --> 06:57.330
Try your best, Usato!

06:57.330 --> 06:59.880
Your legs are shaking, Usato!

06:59.880 --> 07:02.960
There won't be any lunch for 
you if you're too slow, Usato!

07:03.500 --> 07:06.560
Hey, I see a little bug who's a lap behind.

07:07.280 --> 07:09.420
<i>I want to talk back!</i>

07:09.420 --> 07:11.980
<i>I'll write this in my journal, too!</i>

07:11.990 --> 07:15.910
<b>Day 5</b>

07:11.990 --> 07:15.910
<b>Day 5</b>

07:12.710 --> 07:15.900
<i>Day five. I ran all day again.</i>

07:19.620 --> 07:22.330
<b>Day 6</b>

07:19.620 --> 07:22.330
<b>Day 6</b>

07:20.310 --> 07:21.910
<i>Day six. I ran.</i>

07:22.560 --> 07:25.430
Hey, little bug! You're slowing down!

07:28.940 --> 07:31.720
<i>You cold-hearted witch!</i>

07:32.080 --> 07:34.140
<i>I'll write about you in my journal!</i>

07:36.800 --> 07:38.450
<i>What's this?</i>

07:39.470 --> 07:41.890
<i>The light of healing magic?</i>

07:42.260 --> 07:45.820
<i>Do I need this right now? Not really, right?</i>

07:48.730 --> 07:50.650
<b>Day 7</b>

07:48.730 --> 07:50.650
<b>Day 7</b>

07:51.350 --> 07:53.430
Never had my ass kicked like this before!

07:54.810 --> 07:57.960
<i>Day seven. I ran again 
until I thought I'd die.</i>

07:57.960 --> 07:59.450
<i>Then she kicked my ass.</i>

08:01.200 --> 08:03.840
You're pissing me off, 
so we're raising the difficulty.

08:04.170 --> 08:05.960
<i>What?! What the hell?</i>

08:05.540 --> 08:08.250
...cold-hearted witch.
Looks like I'm in for more tomorrow...

08:05.960 --> 08:08.260
<i>Did she find out I was 
dissing her in my journal?</i>

08:08.260 --> 08:12.750
<i>No, she can't read Japanese. 
Is it showing on my face?</i>

08:13.400 --> 08:16.100
Come on, don't just lie there!

08:14.480 --> 08:16.100
H-H-Hold on a second!

08:16.390 --> 08:18.090
Run!

08:18.090 --> 08:22.030
<i>I'm going to call her a vicious 
muscle-bound gorilla in my journal!</i>

08:22.020 --> 08:23.940
<b>Day 8</b>

08:22.020 --> 08:23.940
<b>Day 8</b>

08:22.370 --> 08:26.280
<i>Day eight. I never learn.</i>

08:26.980 --> 08:30.400
<b>Day 9</b>

08:26.980 --> 08:30.400
<b>Day 9</b>

08:26.990 --> 08:29.730
A kick that hard could lead to serious injury!

08:30.700 --> 08:36.000
<i>Day nine. I questioned the need for 
healing light a few days ago, but...</i>

08:36.000 --> 08:37.780
I'm gonna die.

08:37.780 --> 08:40.200
My ass is gonna die.

08:40.200 --> 08:41.110
Huh?

08:41.750 --> 08:43.510
It doesn't hurt.

08:44.660 --> 08:47.510
Not just my butt, but my whole body.

08:48.320 --> 08:50.760
Is this healing magic?

08:50.760 --> 08:53.590
<i>I was wrong about healing magic.</i>

08:53.590 --> 08:56.860
<i>I really, really need it...</i>

09:01.270 --> 09:04.180
<b>Day 10</b>

09:01.270 --> 09:04.180
<b>Day 10</b>

09:01.900 --> 09:06.710
<i>Day ten. Now that I can manifest 
healing magic on demand,</i>

09:06.710 --> 09:09.480
<i>I don't get tired no matter how much I run.</i>

09:10.310 --> 09:12.840
<i>But I keep getting uneasy.</i>

09:12.840 --> 09:15.070
<i>All I'm doing is running around every day.</i>

09:15.070 --> 09:18.830
<i>Will I really be able to help 
Kazuki and Inukami-senpai?</i>

09:19.830 --> 09:23.280
<i>I'm sure Ms. Rose would deck 
me if voiced my concerns.</i>

09:24.260 --> 09:26.670
Hey, Usato! Add thirty laps!

09:27.560 --> 09:29.550
And pick up the pace!

09:30.130 --> 09:32.220
<i>I'm not calling her "Ms. Rose" anymore!</i>

09:32.530 --> 09:35.390
<i>She doesn't deserve any more than just "Rose"!</i>

09:35.390 --> 09:38.860
<i>For now, I have to finish my training!</i>

09:38.860 --> 09:42.460
<i>After that, I'll rip Rose a new one!</i>

09:42.470 --> 09:48.400
<b>Day 11</b>

09:42.470 --> 09:48.400
<b>Day 11</b>

09:42.750 --> 09:44.530
<i>Day eleven.</i>

09:43.000 --> 09:48.380
814... 815... 816...

09:44.530 --> 09:47.370
<i>There was a new addition
to the training regimen today.</i>

09:48.780 --> 09:54.160
817... 818...

09:55.640 --> 09:58.790
819... 820... 821...

09:58.170 --> 10:02.320
Hey, Usato. Do you know why you're 
training your body like this?

09:58.790 --> 10:01.850
822... 823... 824...

10:01.850 --> 10:03.740
825...

10:03.740 --> 10:07.750
826... 827... 828...

10:03.740 --> 10:07.750
It's so you can run from the enemy 
as quickly as possible in battle.

10:08.100 --> 10:09.620
<i>In battle?</i>

10:09.620 --> 10:12.860
It's also so you can save your injured allies.

10:12.860 --> 10:16.040
The faster you run, 
the faster you can save them.

10:16.320 --> 10:20.350
The faster I run, 
the faster I can save them...

10:20.350 --> 10:21.950
Hey, don't stop.

10:21.950 --> 10:23.100
Oh, right!

10:23.990 --> 10:27.800
<i>I finished training without getting
 scolded too much today.</i>

10:23.990 --> 10:27.980
829... 830... 831... 832...

10:27.800 --> 10:31.480
<i>I should be thrilled, but it was pretty scary.</i>

10:27.980 --> 10:31.930
833... 834... 835... 836

10:31.940 --> 10:35.860
<b>Day 12</b>

10:31.940 --> 10:35.860
<b>Day 12</b>

10:32.310 --> 10:37.520
<i>Day twelve. I ran until the afternoon 
and then did push-ups into the night.</i>

10:38.270 --> 10:41.300
<i>I think my body feels lighter.</i>

10:42.600 --> 10:48.100
<i>Day thirteen. Rose apparently caught 
on to that and added weights.</i>

10:42.620 --> 10:45.540
<b>Day 13</b>

10:42.620 --> 10:45.540
<b>Day 13</b>

10:48.570 --> 10:51.230
<i>It's really heavy...</i>

10:52.380 --> 10:54.800
<b>Day 14</b>

10:52.380 --> 10:54.800
<b>Day 14</b>

10:52.710 --> 10:53.980
<i>Day fourteen.</i>

10:54.810 --> 10:56.650
<i>My lunch went missing.</i>

10:57.210 --> 10:58.290
Hurry it up!

10:57.860 --> 11:00.620
Has anyone seen my boxed lunch?

11:00.620 --> 11:02.160
I left it right here.

11:02.160 --> 11:04.390
I just went to get some water...

11:05.710 --> 11:08.170
Oh, I ate it.

11:08.790 --> 11:11.300
What? That was yours?

11:12.140 --> 11:15.900
I thought somebody left it 
because they didn't want it.

11:15.900 --> 11:18.020
Sorry 'bout that!

11:18.020 --> 11:19.740
Are you kidding me?!

11:20.360 --> 11:22.110
Hey, calm down.

11:22.110 --> 11:24.570
You freaking thief!

11:24.040 --> 11:24.950
Hey, now...

11:25.260 --> 11:28.340
Don't you know infighting is 
banned in the Rescue Team?

11:28.340 --> 11:29.280
Like I care!

11:29.280 --> 11:30.580
Whoopsies!

11:30.020 --> 11:34.370
Hold it right there! Just one punch!
I'm gonna deck you good!

11:33.880 --> 11:37.220
<i>I got used to the weights right away.</i>

11:34.370 --> 11:35.640
You think I'm stupid?

11:37.220 --> 11:40.350
<i>I feel like I'm actually 
getting the hang of things.</i>

11:41.830 --> 11:45.320
<i>Wait, is it possible I'm being brainwashed?</i>

11:45.720 --> 11:48.640
<b>Day 21</b>

11:45.720 --> 11:48.640
<b>Day 21</b>

11:46.080 --> 11:52.070
<i>A week later, Kazuki and 
Inukami-senpai came to visit.</i>

11:58.220 --> 12:00.070
Usato's over there.

12:00.310 --> 12:01.700
Thank you very much.

12:05.520 --> 12:08.140
Wait, that's Usato?

12:17.450 --> 12:22.610
Hey, you're slowing down again. 
Have you turned into a caterpillar?

12:23.220 --> 12:25.850
Don't whine about something this easy.

12:25.850 --> 12:29.770
Who the hell is whining?!

12:29.770 --> 12:32.420
No prattling.

12:34.350 --> 12:36.220
Did you just click your tongue at me?

12:36.220 --> 12:40.700
You're so light that I couldn't 
help myself, Ms. Rose...

12:40.700 --> 12:45.140
My, what a smooth talker.

12:47.220 --> 12:49.320
If that's how it is...

13:01.420 --> 13:05.810
You're finally starting to 
become my kind of man.

13:07.070 --> 13:10.720
Looks like I'll be able to take you 
out there sooner than I thought.

13:11.380 --> 13:12.470
No way...

13:12.470 --> 13:14.890
Is that really Usato-kun?

13:16.310 --> 13:18.400
What amazing muscles!

13:18.400 --> 13:20.330
Yeah, this training is brutal...

13:21.010 --> 13:21.990
Huh?

13:22.150 --> 13:25.990
<i>The Wrong Way to Use Healing Magic</i>

13:26.330 --> 13:28.810
What do you think you're doing?!

13:30.400 --> 13:32.900
I asked you what in the world you're doing!

13:33.350 --> 13:36.470
You're destroying a young 
man with a bright future!

13:37.050 --> 13:39.900
Let go, old man Siglis.

13:39.900 --> 13:42.960
Your knightly ideals are impressive,

13:42.960 --> 13:45.830
but I have my own way of doing things.

13:46.490 --> 13:49.910
Usato is going to become my right-hand man.

13:49.910 --> 13:52.730
It'll be a real problem if
 he can't handle this much.

13:53.400 --> 13:55.350
Your right-hand man?

13:55.350 --> 13:57.760
<i>Her right-hand man?!</i>

13:58.030 --> 14:00.410
He's a real find.

14:00.410 --> 14:02.840
I love how he can't stand to lose.

14:02.840 --> 14:05.370
The way he never gives up is even better.

14:05.370 --> 14:10.340
And on top of all that, 
he's been able to survive my training.

14:11.680 --> 14:12.730
<i>Huh?</i>

14:12.730 --> 14:16.760
<i>Wait, did wanting to show her
 a thing or two backfire on me?</i>

14:16.760 --> 14:20.130
Usato, take a break and get some lunch.

14:20.130 --> 14:22.340
I'm sure you want to catch 
up with the heroes.

14:22.340 --> 14:23.630
Uh... Okay.

14:27.790 --> 14:31.080
Dame Suzune and Sir Kazuki, 
please take care of Princess Celia.

14:31.080 --> 14:33.630
I need to speak further with this woman.

14:34.020 --> 14:37.180
U-Understood. Let's go, Usato.

14:37.180 --> 14:38.190
Yeah...

14:39.270 --> 14:41.710
I knew you were a deviant!

14:41.710 --> 14:46.020
I was ordered to re-enlist you,
 but I can't accept your transfer!

14:46.600 --> 14:48.490
It's not happening either way.

14:48.490 --> 14:50.530
My right eye is totally useless.

14:50.530 --> 14:52.160
Don't talk nonsense!

14:52.990 --> 14:56.410
Huh? That guy commands
the Llinger Kingdom's army?

14:56.410 --> 14:59.980
Yeah. That's Commander Siglis, 
the strongest knight in the kingdom.

14:59.980 --> 15:02.910
He's teaching us sword fighting.

15:02.910 --> 15:05.530
Really? That's awesome.

15:06.010 --> 15:08.090
By the way, who is this young lady?

15:09.340 --> 15:14.360
Pardon me. My name is Celia Vulgast Llinger.

15:14.650 --> 15:16.120
Llinger?

15:16.120 --> 15:19.370
Wait, does that make you the king's...

15:19.370 --> 15:21.110
Yes, I am his daughter.

15:21.110 --> 15:23.340
Y-You're a princess?!

15:23.340 --> 15:27.410
F-Forgive me for my uncouth conduct!

15:27.770 --> 15:30.330
Please, no need to be formal with me.

15:30.330 --> 15:32.790
Huh? Is that okay? Really?

15:32.790 --> 15:35.110
Yes, I would like that much more.

15:35.830 --> 15:39.570
You're acting just like Kazuki-kun 
did in the beginning.

15:39.570 --> 15:43.080
P-Please stop, Inukami-senpai!

15:44.310 --> 15:50.950
Um, I brought this for everyone. 
I hope you'll enjoy it.

15:55.560 --> 15:57.460
It's super delicious!

15:58.600 --> 16:00.270
Thank you very much.

16:00.700 --> 16:02.350
Hey, Usato.

16:02.350 --> 16:06.440
Do you undergo training like that every day?

16:06.440 --> 16:10.080
Nah, today's training was pretty light.

16:10.080 --> 16:12.410
How are things on your end?

16:12.410 --> 16:16.460
Huh? Well... um...

16:16.880 --> 16:19.430
The training itself is pretty difficult,

16:19.430 --> 16:25.390
but Commander Siglis and Ms. Welcie always 
consider our health and well-being

16:25.390 --> 16:29.040
while teaching us how to 
use our swords and magic.

16:29.040 --> 16:30.350
I see.

16:30.350 --> 16:32.310
Well, that's how it should be.

16:32.310 --> 16:34.380
Ms. Rose is really brutal.

16:34.380 --> 16:36.020
I'm sorry, Usato.

16:36.020 --> 16:38.270
Why are you apologizing, Kazuki?

16:38.270 --> 16:39.470
Oh, let me get another!

16:42.420 --> 16:44.270
Hey, Usato...

16:44.830 --> 16:46.800
Just a quick peek, Usato-kun!

16:46.800 --> 16:48.430
S-S-S-Senpai?!

16:49.360 --> 16:52.360
I knew it! Just look at those muscles!

16:52.600 --> 16:55.880
Usato-kun, let me touch them a bit!

16:55.880 --> 16:56.790
What?!

16:56.790 --> 16:58.740
H-H-Hold on, Senpai! Calm down!

16:58.740 --> 16:59.840
Whoa, whoa.

16:59.840 --> 17:02.280
Kazuki was about to say 
something! Weren't you?!

17:02.280 --> 17:04.640
No, I, well...

17:06.260 --> 17:09.200
Isn't it tough for you, Usato?

17:12.070 --> 17:14.140
It's crazy tough.

17:14.140 --> 17:16.940
In the beginning, I kept wanting to run away.

17:16.940 --> 17:18.860
Do you feel differently now?

17:19.140 --> 17:23.020
Ms. Rose is scary, but I don't 
want to run away anymore.

17:23.490 --> 17:27.010
The training is starting to get fun, too.

17:27.640 --> 17:30.890
Life here isn't that bad.

17:32.030 --> 17:34.330
You're amazing, Usato-kun.

17:34.710 --> 17:37.140
You've already found your place.

17:37.140 --> 17:39.360
It's not amazing.

17:39.360 --> 17:41.360
I'm just stubborn.

17:42.280 --> 17:46.310
The two of you are going to 
fight as heroes someday.

17:46.310 --> 17:49.200
I want to be able to do what I can.

17:52.770 --> 17:57.060
Then can I count on you to come 
save me if I'm ever in trouble?

17:57.060 --> 18:02.390
Listen, even if you suddenly 
start talking like a normal girl...

18:02.390 --> 18:04.540
I <i>am</i> a normal girl!

18:04.540 --> 18:07.020
Just what do you take me for?

18:07.020 --> 18:11.290
I have to agree that you could hardly 
call Ms. Suzune a normal girl.

18:11.290 --> 18:13.840
What?! Not you too, Princess Celia!

18:14.490 --> 18:17.650
Hey, there you are, Usato.

18:17.650 --> 18:22.400
I was kind enough to bring you some lunch.

18:22.820 --> 18:27.340
Why are you talking like 
you're doing me a big favor?

18:27.620 --> 18:32.920
How shameless do you have to be to 
bring me my lunch?! You blockhead!

18:33.460 --> 18:37.480
You're still holding a grudge over 
something that's in the past?

18:37.480 --> 18:38.680
Are you a little kid?

18:38.680 --> 18:41.840
I don't want to hear that from the guy...

18:42.350 --> 18:45.130
who stole that kid's lunch!

18:44.020 --> 18:46.200
Bring it on, asshole!

18:46.200 --> 18:49.230
The boss ain't around today! 
I'll beat the crap out of you!

18:51.580 --> 18:53.740
I'd like to see you try!

18:53.740 --> 18:56.010
Rotten little brat!

18:57.020 --> 18:58.090
Musclehead!

18:58.090 --> 18:59.710
Baby chick!

18:58.240 --> 19:00.290
Wh-What should we do?

19:02.670 --> 19:04.820
It's fine, Princess Celia.

19:07.240 --> 19:10.270
I think this is just part 
of Usato's daily life.

19:11.070 --> 19:12.260
I agree.

19:12.260 --> 19:14.810
He lives each day here freely as himself.

19:14.810 --> 19:18.100
He's may have acclimated
far better than we did.

19:18.100 --> 19:20.320
I'm feeling a bit restless now.

19:21.260 --> 19:23.430
I'm heading back to the castle to train.

19:23.430 --> 19:24.270
Huh?

19:24.270 --> 19:27.420
Oh, Sir Kazuki, please wait!

19:31.660 --> 19:38.040
<i>I believe there's a reason the three 
of us were summoned here together.</i>

19:39.120 --> 19:42.240
<i>Let's do our best together, Usato-kun.</i>

19:43.200 --> 19:44.660
Hot, hot, hot...

19:47.240 --> 19:51.310
<i>It was great to see Kazuki 
and Inukami-senpai...</i>

19:51.310 --> 19:55.070
<i>even if Senpai's behavior 
kinda freaked me out.</i>

19:56.460 --> 19:59.650
<i>But what she said was true.</i>

20:00.270 --> 20:03.210
<i>My body really has changed.</i>

20:03.210 --> 20:05.680
<i>I've gotten a lot faster, too.</i>

20:06.340 --> 20:09.300
<i>I've been healing my muscles
over and over again after</i>

20:09.300 --> 20:11.100
<i>they're damaged by strenuous training.</i>

20:11.400 --> 20:13.910
<i>This is the result.</i>

20:14.400 --> 20:15.320
<i>Except...</i>

20:15.780 --> 20:19.180
The faster you run, 
the faster you can save them.

20:19.770 --> 20:23.140
<i>You have to run to save the 
injured on the battlefield.</i>

20:23.140 --> 20:25.610
<i>But can someone like me really do that?</i>

20:26.380 --> 20:31.110
<i>Do I have the mental fortitude 
to match this body I've built?</i>

20:33.690 --> 20:36.450
Usato, we're going out today.

20:36.450 --> 20:37.600
Okay...

20:39.010 --> 20:40.420
They're going out?

20:40.420 --> 20:42.250
So it's finally time...

20:44.090 --> 20:45.750
<i>Wait, what?</i>

20:45.750 --> 20:49.920
C-Captain Rose, wh-what brings you here today?

20:49.920 --> 20:51.720
Hey, Thomas.

20:51.720 --> 20:54.490
I want to show my subordinate 
the outside world.

20:54.490 --> 20:56.310
Urk! I'll get the gate right now!

20:56.310 --> 20:57.100
Good.

20:57.100 --> 20:59.010
<i>That's Rose for you.</i>

20:57.100 --> 21:00.260
Hey! Captain Rose is passing through!
Help me! Hurry it up!

20:59.010 --> 21:01.600
<i>She just has to stand there to scare someone.</i>

21:01.600 --> 21:03.940
<i>Anyway, what's this about the outside world?</i>

21:13.480 --> 21:16.930
Ms. Rose, where are we going?

21:16.930 --> 21:18.660
Just shut up and follow.

21:21.970 --> 21:23.220
We're here.

21:23.730 --> 21:27.100
This forest is also known 
as the Darkness of Llinger.

21:27.100 --> 21:29.980
It's infamously teeming with monsters.

21:30.410 --> 21:34.460
Don't come back until you 
hunt down a grand grizzly.

21:34.460 --> 21:35.080
Huh?!

21:35.080 --> 21:36.440
H-H-H-Hang on a minute!

21:36.440 --> 21:40.890
Blue grizzlies only turn into grand grizzlies
 after living a hundred years!

21:40.890 --> 21:45.280
And that book said even 
blue grizzlies are really dangerous!

21:45.550 --> 21:49.070
You should be able to take one 
down easily now. Understand?

21:49.070 --> 21:50.530
Not at all!

21:50.530 --> 21:53.310
All I've done is run!
I don't know how to fight!

21:53.740 --> 21:55.620
You are such a pain.

21:55.620 --> 21:58.460
Wait, no! Stop! Don't lift me up!

21:58.460 --> 22:02.460
A-And don't wind up!
